// NPC melee damage and the offscreen reduction. Original rule (melee.md, decoded): an NPC slash deals
// round(m_fAttackDamageMultiplier 1.0 x Attribute_MeleeDamage of the guard's sword) = 10 / 15 / 20 / 30
// (Easy / Normal / Hard / Very Hard, Twk_Inv_SwordEliteGuard), and when the attacker is "effectively
// offscreen" (behind the camera) the damage is x (1 - DishonoredPlayerPawn.m_fOffscreenMeleeDamageReduction
// 0.5) = 7.5 -> 8 on Normal. HOOK_TRIAGE.md 2026-10-06 recorded 15 and 8 on some first hits.
// Here the player faces away (yaw 180) and the guard comes from behind (alerted, 300 uu).
(
    name: "combat/melee_guard_offscreen",
    system: Combat,
    map: "Playground",
    description: "An alerted guard attacks the player from behind (offscreen): first hit 8 on Normal, front hit 15 (combat/guard_attack).",
    setup: (
        player: Some((position: (-5600, 0, 96), yaw: 180)),
        npcs: [(id: Some("guard"), position: Some((-5300, 0, 92)), yaw: 180, state: Some("Alerted"))],
        settle: 1,
    ),
    ticks: 900,
    input: [],
    checkpoints: [
        (name: "first hit while offscreen", expect: [(metric: EventValue("Sim:Damage@player[cause=Sword]", "amount"), value: 8, tol: 0.5, source: "Twk_Inv_SwordEliteGuard MeleeDamage Normal 15 x (1 - 0.5), rounded (0x00C33DD0, DishonoredPlayerPawn defaults); the port gives 14", status: Static)]),
    ],
    record: [Pawn, Vitals, Npc("guard"), SimEvents],
    capture: Some("measure sword npc=<doorman> --defend 10 with the player facing away; record each damage-path call amount"),
)